TASK REFACTOR59
	TITLE "the repository guards read files, import specifiers and corpus lines through shared"
		+ "modules"
	STATUS todo
	SPEC "the file walk of the shared script port scans the root it receives, never process.cwd():"
		+ "a guard run from another directory reports the same violations as one run from the root"
	SPEC "the reading of import specifiers, static and dynamic, is declared once and used by"
		+ "check:presentation and check:dependencies"
	SPEC "the filter of generated directories is declared once and used by every guard that skips"
		+ "them"
	SPEC "no guard imports from another guard: the reading of corpus lines used by check:anchors"
		+ "and check:audit-ignores lives in a shared module"
	SPEC "the main function of a script returns its exit code and no port carries an exit:"
		+ "runAsEntryPoint alone calls process.exit, and a script test asserts the returned code"
	SPEC "the script port is split by responsibility, files apart from console, and no guard"
		+ "receives a port member it never calls"
	SPEC "a script test reading a file the fake does not hold fails naming that path"
	SPEC "a guard fails when a check-*.ts file of scripts/ imports Glob or readdir"
	SPEC "the helpers the guards share live in scripts/helpers/, one file per responsibility, and"
		+ "neither scripts/specSources.ts nor scripts/scriptIo.ts exists"
	SPEC "the guards decision and the script injection decision name scripts/helpers/ as the place"
		+ "of the shared helpers, their IMPL anchors following them"
	SPEC "on the repository at the base commit, every guard reports the same violations and exits"
		+ "with the same code as before the task"
	RATIONALE "The guards decision requires what guards share to be declared once in a common"
		+ "module. Pull request 197 delivered part of it: every guard reads its files through the"
		+ "ScriptIo port of scripts/scriptIo.ts, the only module importing Glob, and"
		+ "check-package-dependencies prints through reportViolations. What remains on that head:"
		+ "the port scans process.cwd() instead of a root it receives; the dynamic import specifier"
		+ "pattern is copied in check-presentation-entities and check-package-dependencies; the"
		+ "generated-directory filter is copied in five guards and specSources; check-audit-ignores"
		+ "imports readCorpusLines and removeQuotes from check-corpus-anchors; scripts/helpers/"
		+ "does not exist. Ruled with the owner on 2026-09-26 after the review of 197: exit leaves"
		+ "the port, the main function returning its code and runAsEntryPoint alone exiting,"
		+ "because a fake exit that returns lets the test run past the point the real process"
		+ "stops; the port is split so that a guard using one member (listTrackedFiles for"
		+ "check:anchors, commandLineArguments for validate:tables) does not receive seven; the"
		+ "fake readText fails on a path it does not hold instead of yielding undefined;"
		+ "runAsEntryPoint and its process adapter stay duplicated in"
		+ "packages/core-mapping/scripts/sectionValidatorsFile.ts, a package importing no root"
		+ "script and the helper package being refused. One pull request, in commits the review"
		+ "reads in order: port and exit, the move to scripts/helpers/, the shared readings, the"
		+ "Glob guard; each green on bun test and bun run guards. No helper package is created:"
		+ "every consumer lives in scripts/, which is no package. The name specSources dates from"
		+ "pull request 15, when the module served only the guards reading spec files; it now"
		+ "gathers unrelated helpers, hence one file per responsibility. check:section-validators"
		+ "and validate:tables are package scripts and stay out. Distinct from pull request 195,"
		+ "which changed how the guards are run, not the code they share"
		REF @DECISION.RepositoryGuardsAreGroupedScripts
		REF @DECISION.AScriptTestInjectsItsInputAndOutputAndCoverageIgnoresTheRealAdapter
	SOURCE "Raised in the review of pull request 101; refined with the owner on 2026-09-26"
		PR 101
	SOURCE "Re-refined with the owner on 2026-09-26, after the review of pull request 197"
		PR 197

TASK FEAT69
	TITLE "Open a validated save as an editable draft and write the draft to a new save"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "a draft opened from a save and exported without an edit produces the same bytes as the"
		+ "file it was opened from, whichever format that save carries"
	SPEC "an edit operation applied to a draft changes the field it names and nothing else, and the"
		+ "file the draft was opened from is never written"
	SPEC "a draft is validated before it is serialized, by the validator the display and the merge"
		+ "already run, and an invalid draft produces no save"
	WAVE @WAVE.6
	RATIONALE "The display flow keeps the loaded save as its raw text and re-parses it once per"
		+ "section, so nothing holds a save an edit could reach; the serializer is reachable from"
		+ "the merge alone, and every domain entity is read-only. An editable draft is therefore a"
		+ "use case of core-mapping beside MergeSaveFiles, holding the parsed sections, taking"
		+ "typed operations and giving back a new save text, so that the user interface holds edit"
		+ "state and no save format knowledge. Exporting the unedited draft byte for byte is what"
		+ "proves the draft loses nothing the loaded save carried, the float suffix and the int64"
		+ "player identifier first; it closes the key order and unknown property questions the"
		+ "round trip tests leave open. The rest of wave 6 edits fields through this draft"
		REF @PACKAGE.core_mapping
		REF @RULE.FloatFieldsCarryADotZeroSuffixInFlatRecords
		REF @RULE.APlayerIdentifierIsCarriedAsExactDecimalText
		REF @RULE.ASectionLineIsOneJsonEntry
		REF @DECISION.ValidationIsTheSingleSourceOfWarnings
		REF @DECISION.DissolvedPackagesAreNotRecreated
		REF @TASK.FEAT71
	SOURCE "Wave 6 rewritten on the owner ruling of 2026-09-21 rejecting the tasks of pull request"
		+ "108: the save manager gains an edit mode, every field it displays becomes editable, each"
		+ "case designed on its own"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Round trip measured on 2026-09-21 at commit c65c7cb over the three valid scenario"
		+ "fixtures: parse then serialize returns the exact bytes of baseline_valid.json and"
		+ "other-player_valid.json, and returns 2538 bytes against 2620 for"
		+ "legacy-format_valid.json, whose terrain layers section the normalization drops"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

TASK FEAT70
	TITLE "Offer a save built in the browser as a new file under a name distinct from the loaded"
		+ "one"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "a save content built in the browser is offered for download as a new file whose name"
		+ "derives from the loaded one and differs from it, the loaded file being left untouched"
	SPEC "the merge result offers its merged save through that same path, under the name it carries"
		+ "today"
	SPEC "offering a second content releases the link of the first"
	WAVE @WAVE.6
	RATIONALE "The merge result is the one place a save built in the browser reaches the user, as a"
		+ "blob behind a download link whose object URL is revoked on every new result, and the"
		+ "display flow has no such path. The edit mode of wave 6 and the save repair of wave 7"
		+ "both end on a new file the user downloads, so the path is extracted once from the merge"
		+ "result rather than written a second and a third time. It is a task of its own so that"
		+ "neither wave waits for the other: the repair view depends on this task and on nothing"
		+ "else of wave 6"
		REF @PACKAGE.ui_save_manager
		REF @TASK.FEAT71
		REF @TASK.FEAT80
	SOURCE "Wave 6 rewritten on the owner ruling of 2026-09-21 rejecting the tasks of pull request"
		+ "108: the edit mode and the save repair each create a new save file and never overwrite"
		+ "the loaded one"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST
	SOURCE "Read on 2026-09-21 at commit c65c7cb: the merge result section builds the blob, the"
		+ "object URL and the download link and revokes the URL on each new result and on cleanup,"
		+ "and the merged file name is built from the sanitised stems of the two loaded files"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

