TASK FEAT75
	TITLE "Edit a player, their equipment and their inventory as grids of slots"
	STATUS draft
	SPEC "the inventory and the equipment of a player are displayed as a grid of as many cells as"
		+ "the size of that inventory declares, an item per cell, the empty cells shown"
	SPEC "an item is added into an empty cell only, from the catalogue, and the save gains a world"
		+ "object whose identifier is above every inventory and world object identifier it carries"
	SPEC "removing an item drops it from the inventory and from the world objects of the save, and"
		+ "replacing an item is a removal followed by an addition in the same cell"
	SPEC "an item the loaded save carries with a quantity keeps that quantity through an edit of"
		+ "the inventory it sits in"
	SPEC "the player name is edited and carries its new value into the exported save"
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT69
	AFTER @TASK.FEAT74
	WAVE @WAVE.6
	RATIONALE "An inventory names its items by identifier and declares a size nothing checks, so a"
		+ "free list would let a save be written with more items than the inventory holds; a grid"
		+ "of exactly size cells makes that save unrepresentable rather than refused after the"
		+ "fact. Adding an item mints an identifier above the maximum of the two sections sharing"
		+ "the numbering space, as the merge sequence does, uniqueness over the union being no"
		+ "property of a save the game itself writes. The display resolves an item identifier to"
		+ "its world object name and drops the identifier, so the section needs a reader carrying"
		+ "the cell, the identifier and the name. Removing an item drops the world object too, no"
		+ "reader tolerating an inventory naming an identifier no world object carries"
		REF @SECTION.Inventories
		REF @SECTION.WorldObjects
		REF @SECTION.Players
		REF @RULE.IdentifiersAreSharedByInventoriesAndWorldObjects
		REF @TASK.FEAT74
		REF @TASK.FEAT69
	SOURCE "Wave 6 rewritten on the owner ruling of 2026-09-21 rejecting the tasks of pull request"
		+ "108: a view of its own for an inventory, a grid whose cell is a slot, so that nothing"
		+ "can be added beyond the limit of the inventory"
		REF @PROJECT.PCST

